    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3845835e-41d5-5887-b90d-1b41973eb3fe",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
